cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "pollination-morphology: mechanical isolation from computed pollen placement"
abstract: >-
  A simulation in which where a flower deposits pollen on a pollinator is
  computed from flower and body geometry rather than set as a trait, so that
  mechanical reproductive isolation can arise — or fail to — for inspectable
  reasons. Includes an individual-based model with inheritance and
  recombination, and pre-registered tests of temporal assortment, spatial
  structure, evolving flowering width, and reproductive assurance.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jaret
    family-names: Arnold
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4055-5238"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-11"
# NOTE: this repository is dual-licensed BY FILE CLASS, and CFF 1.2.0 cannot express that.
# `license` does accept a list, but the CFF schema states that multiple licences are read as
# OR, not AND ("When there are multiple licenses, it is assumed their relationship is OR") —
# which would wrongly tell a reader they may take the WHOLE work under either one. The real
# position is AND, split by file class, so a single identifier plus this note is the closest
# honest encoding:
#   MIT        -> the CODE: sim/, tools/, tests/, experiments/**/*.js, *.html  (see LICENSE)
#   CC-BY-4.0  -> the PROSE, figures and data tables under docs/ and
#                 experiments/**/*.md                                    (see LICENSE-docs)
# The authoritative file-class table is in README.md. If you reuse the text, a figure or a
# data table rather than the software, CC-BY-4.0 is the licence that governs.
#
# `license-url` is deliberately NOT set: the schema documents it as "only for non-standard
# licenses not included in the SPDX License List", and both MIT and CC-BY-4.0 are SPDX
# identifiers. It is also a single value, so it could not carry both in any case.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/musharna/pollination-morphology"
url: "https://musharna.github.io/pollination-morphology/"
keywords:
